    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\tfrac12v^2)=v\\dfrac{dv}{dx}=\\dfrac{dv}{dt}$. Apply the chain rule to $v(x)$, then use $\\frac{dx}{dt}=v$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(\\frac12v^2\\right)&=v\\frac{dv}{dx}\\\\\\frac{dv}{dt}&=\\frac{dv}{dx}\\frac{dx}{dt}\\\\\\frac{dv}{dt}&=v\\frac{dv}{dx}.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\tfrac12v^2)=v\\dfrac{dv}{dx}=\\dfrac{dv}{dt}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
